+A V8 isolate is bound to the thread that created it, so the overlap does not
+come from re-entering one isolate — Shape gives TypeScript **four dedicated
+worker threads, each owning its own isolate**. Two consequences worth knowing:
+at most four `async fn typescript` calls run at once and a fifth queues, and
+module-level state in an async TypeScript body is per-worker rather than shared
+across every call.
+
+The extension embeds a bare `deno_core` runtime with no web platform
+extensions, so browser globals such as `setTimeout` and `fetch` are not defined.
